    "definition": "R_shear is the DES-weighted mean of the per-object finite-difference matrix on no-shear-selected rows. R_sel[:,j] = (weighted mean of noshear shapes on branch +j selection minus weighted mean of noshear shapes on branch -j selection)/(2*0.01), normalising each branch separately. R_total=R_shear+R_sel. R_joint is included only as a separate diagnostic, not substituted for R_total.",
